leftmargin rightmargin pagey 12 TextStart
/TextFont /Helvetica findfont text_size scalefont def
(The single-port ROM has\
 chip enable \(CEN\),\
 address \(A\),\
 and data out \(Q\) pins.\
 The memory is self-timed and consumes the minimum amount of power for read operation.) TextLine
TextEnd
/pagey exch def
() TextLine
% spaceLeft beginning paragraph 186
leftmargin rightmargin pagey 12 TextStart
/TextFont /Helvetica findfont text_size scalefont def
() TextLine
(The read address \(A\) and read chip enable \(CEN\) are latched on the rising-edge\
 of the clock \(CLK\).) TextLine
() TextLine
(When CEN is high the memory is deselected and forced into a low-power standby mode.\
 The existing data outputs continue to drive their previous values.) TextLine
TextEnd
/pagey exch def


% spaceLeft beginning paragraph 120
leftmargin rightmargin pagey 12 TextStart
/TextFont /Helvetica findfont text_size scalefont def
() TextLine
(The Self timing overrride STOV allows you to\
 adjust the latching of output in posedge or negedge of the clock.) TextLine
TextEnd
/pagey exch def

% spaceLeft beginning paragraph 90
leftmargin rightmargin pagey 12 TextStart
/TextFont /Helvetica findfont text_size scalefont def
() TextLine
(If the KEN=0, the keepers on the bitlines will be enabled. This will\
slow-down the access time. If the KEN=1, the keepers on the bitlines will be disabled.) TextLine
TextEnd
/pagey exch def

% spaceLeft beginning paragraph 60
leftmargin rightmargin pagey 12 TextStart
/TextFont /Helvetica findfont text_size scalefont def
() TextLine
(The Extra Margin Adjustment EMA allows you to\
 adjust the width of the self timing pulse.) TextLine
TextEnd
/pagey exch def

